{"skill":{"slug":"debug-pro","displayName":"Debug Pro"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769625005426,"changelog":"debug-pro 1.0.0 initial release:\n\n- Introduces a detailed 7-step debugging protocol for systematic problem-solving.\n- Provides quick-reference debugging commands for JavaScript/TypeScript, Python, Swift, CSS/layout, network tools, and git bisect.\n- Includes a table of common error messages, their likely causes, and quick fixes.\n- Lists frequently used diagnostic shell commands for system and application troubleshooting.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3362,"sha256":"88d58b65a81f7ddaf8792716cfb1b44c585e66682e873c82aab3ac180f83fd68","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1537,"sha256":"6778783c6ff478118cb03ebdb9a2dd22844b3aa45d2cf3761343dd9a38dce055","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789022899545,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5989bc409d8d0ce63b05660f3fc4f485b9ff0029914f2a6a0ac9a579d319f35f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5989bc409d8d0ce63b05660f3fc4f485b9ff0029914f2a6a0ac9a579d319f35f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: debug-pro\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle 'debug-pro' is a documentation of debugging methodologies and language-specific commands. It contains numerous examples of legitimate shell commands for system diagnostics, network inspection, and code debugging (e.g., `curl`, `lsof`, `netstat`, `ps aux`, `git bisect`). While these commands involve system access, they are directly aligned with the stated purpose of a debugging skill. There is no evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the AI agent in the `SKILL.md` file. The commands are presented as educational examples, not as instructions for harmful execution.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160227024},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":12,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789022899545},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a debugging reference skill with example commands, not a tool that installs code or runs hidden actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Some examples would inspect local processes, ports, disk, or network endpoints if a user chose to run them, but those diagnostics are coherent with debugging and are shown as examples rather than automatic behavior.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install script, dependency manifest, executable component, or runtime hook was present; metadata was empty and the package inspected was a single Markdown skill file.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are scoped to user-directed debugging workflows and do not attempt to override agent behavior, hide instructions, alter safety constraints, or require automatic execution.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence, credential use, background worker, privilege escalation flow, or durable system modification is instructed; the single mention of sudo appears only as a possible permission-denied troubleshooting consideration.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact's stated purpose is systematic debugging guidance, and the contents are debugging steps, language-specific debugger commands, network diagnostics, git bisect usage, and common error triage.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want a compact debugging checklist and command reference. Review commands before running them, especially network probes and local process or system diagnostics, because they can reveal environment details or contact the named host you target.","findings":"[E1] expected: The flagged external URL appears in example curl commands for HTTP debugging using example domains, with no instruction to transmit secrets or collect user data.\n[PE2] expected: The flagged sudo text is not a root-execution command; it is a word in a troubleshooting table for permission-denied errors.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789022899545}}}}}